"Let $q$ be odd, and let $C$ be a linear MDS code with parameters $[q+1,k]$ over $\\mathbb{F}_q$. Its covering radius is denoted by $\\rho(C)$.\n\n**General covering-radius conjecture.** For $2\\le k\\le q-2$,\n\n$$\n\\rho(C)=q-k.\n$$\n\nThis extends the covering-radius conjecture from projective Reed–Solomon codes to every MDS code of the longest conjecturally possible length $q+1$. It is known in several parameter ranges; the source notes that non-PRS MDS codes exist, so the claim does not follow formally from the projective Reed–Solomon case."